-- ── story 4-9a: B2B freight dispatch ─────────────────────────────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the freight_loads, freight_consignments and
-- freight_load_scans tables, the two order_cartons columns and the twelve
-- indexes — made IF NOT EXISTS by hand, the 6-2a lint) and hand-amended: the
-- fail-fast guard, every CHECK (drizzle-kit is blind to them), the RLS
-- policies (a STAFF-ONLY shape for the load and its scans, the 0041 client
-- clause for the consignment), the attachments, mail, contacts and webhook
-- widenings and the post-migration probes (`bun run db:generate` afterwards
-- reports "No schema changes").
--
-- What changes:
--  * `freight_loads` (A1, A47, A66) — one truck: one warehouse, one
--    transporter, one vehicle, any number of clients' consignments. Staff-only
--    RLS: a client-stamped session sees and writes no row (proved as
--    `wms_rls_probe` in test/freight-dispatch-migration.spec.ts — RLS is inert
--    inside a migration, which runs as the owner; review D20).
--  * `freight_consignments` (A2, A42, A47) — one order on one load; one live
--    consignment per order for ever. RLS with the 0041 client clause.
--  * `freight_load_scans` (A3, A44, A45) — one package scanned onto a load,
--    unique while loaded per (consignment, code). Staff-only RLS.
--  * `order_cartons.package_type` / `inner_count` (A4) — a package is a carton
--    or a pallet (≤ 3,000 kg, "said to contain n cartons").
--  * `attachments` gains the `loading-sheet` purpose on a `freight_load` owner
--    and the `lr` document kind (A5); `email_messages` gains
--    `client-delivery-update`; `client_contacts` gains `delivery.recorded`;
--    `webhook_endpoints` / `webhook_events` gain `order.delivered` (A6).
--
-- No VALIDATE runs here (drift D2, guide §3/§7t): the migrator applies the
-- whole pending set in ONE transaction, so a VALIDATE beside an ADD would scan
-- under the ADD's ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock. `order_cartons` (three),
-- `email_messages` (two) and `webhook_events` (one) are re-added NOT VALID
-- over a superset (asserted below); their VALIDATEs are a post-deploy step
-- (DEPLOY §5, PENDING). `attachments`, `client_contacts` and
-- `webhook_endpoints` are small and re-added validated. 0120 (4-10a) drops
-- and re-adds the attachments, mail and contacts CHECKs BY NAME — the names
-- are a contract. No foreign keys (IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE §3). Additive only.

-- ── 0. fail-fast: already applied, or out of order ──────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'freight_loads') THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0119: freight_loads already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
	IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'order_consignment_records') THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0119 is out of order: order_consignment_records does not exist — 0118 must be applied first.';
	END IF;
END $$;
